  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Let's build this from the ground up not just the technique, but&nbsp;<strong>why it exists</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>what problem it actually solves</strong>.",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-the-problem-that-created-this-pattern",
      "title": "1. The Problem That Created This Pattern",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Imagine you have a linked list. No length variable. No way to know how many nodes are in it. And you need to find the&nbsp;<strong>middle node</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your first instinct:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 1: traverse the whole list to count nodes</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Step 2: traverse again up to count/2</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-222263883.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-222263883.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-222263883.png",
          "alt": "The Problem That Created This Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">First pass: count = 5&nbsp;</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Second pass:&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">stop at 5/2 = 2.5 → position 3 → node [30]</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This works. But you traversed the list&nbsp;<strong>twice</strong>. Two full passes just to find the middle.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Can you do it in&nbsp;<strong>one pass</strong>? Yes. That is exactly what the fast and slow pointer pattern solves.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-the-core-idea",
      "title": "2. The Core Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You put&nbsp;<strong>two pointers</strong>&nbsp;on the list at the same time. Both start at the head. But they move at different speeds:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Slow pointer: moves ONE step at a time</span><br>",
            "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Fast pointer: moves TWO steps at a time</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Because fast moves twice as fast as slow, by the time fast reaches the end of the list, slow has only covered half the distance. Which means<strong>slow is sitting exactly at the middle</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-522605226.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-522605226.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-522605226.png",
          "alt": "The Core Idea"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use two pointers:&nbsp;<strong>slow (S)</strong>&nbsp;moves 1 step,&nbsp;<strong>fast (F)</strong>&nbsp;moves 2 steps,&nbsp;Start both at&nbsp;<strong>[10]</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116559-31534041.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After moves: S → [20] → [30], F → [30] → [50]",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116560-845462958.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116560-845462958.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116560-845462958.png",
          "alt": "The Core Idea"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">When&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">F reaches the end</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">,&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">S is at [30] (middle),&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Fast moves faster, so slow naturally lands in the middle</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"><br></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "One pass. Done.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-why-this-works-the-math",
      "title": "3. Why This Works: The Math",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Think of it like a race on a track. If one runner moves&nbsp;<strong>twice as fast</strong>&nbsp;as the other, then by the time the faster runner finishes the full distance, the slower runner has covered exactly&nbsp;<strong>half the distance</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Fast travels:&nbsp;<strong>n steps</strong>",
            "Slow travels:&nbsp;<strong>n/2 steps</strong>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So when the fast pointer reaches the end of the list, the slow pointer is&nbsp;<strong>n/2 steps from the start</strong>, which is the&nbsp;<strong>middle</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "This isn’t magic it’s just the result of their&nbsp;<strong>speed difference (2:1 ratio)</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4-why-fast-and-slow-works-for-cycles",
      "title": "4. Why Fast and Slow Works for Cycles",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When we use slow and fast pointers, their behavior changes depending on whether a cycle exists.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If there is&nbsp;<strong>no cycle</strong>, the fast pointer keeps moving ahead and eventually reaches&nbsp;<code>null</code>, which means the list ends so we know there is no loop.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "But if there&nbsp;<strong>is a cycle</strong>, the situation becomes like a circular track. Both slow and fast are moving inside this loop, but fast is moving twice as fast.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Because of this speed difference, fast will keep gaining on slow and will eventually catch up to it at some point inside the cycle.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So, if the two pointers ever meet, it means a cycle exists. If fast reaches&nbsp;<code>null</code>, it means there is no cycle.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5-cycle-detection-step-by-step-process",
      "title": "5. Cycle Detection: Step by Step Process",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We use two pointers slow (1 step) and fast (2 steps) to detect a cycle.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 1: Initial State",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116560-229043831.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We start with both pointers at the beginning.<br>slow = A [10] and fast = A [10].",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 2: Iteration 1",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116775-911773449.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Now slow moves one step to B [20].<br>Fast moves two steps to C [30].",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So now: slow = B, fast = C.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 3: Iteration 2",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116776-718300389.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Slow moves one step to C [30].<br>Fast moves two steps to E [50].",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So now: slow = C, fast = E.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "Step 4: Iteration 3",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116776-540027002.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Slow moves one step to D [40].<br>Fast moves two steps: E → C → D.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So now: slow = D, fast = D.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading3",
          "text": "<strong>Step 5: Meeting Point</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406116777-472423586.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Both slow and fast are at the same node [40].<br>This means they have met inside the cycle.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "Since slow and fast meet, a&nbsp;<strong>cycle exists</strong>&nbsp;in the list.<br>If they never met and fast reached null, then there would be&nbsp;<strong>no cycle</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "Node slow = head;\nNode fast = head;\n\nwhile (fast != null && fast.next != null) {\n    slow = slow.next;\n    fast = fast.next.next;\n\n    if (slow == fast) {\n        return true;    // cycle detected\n    }\n}\n\nreturn false;           // fast hit null — no cycle"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Time: O(n):</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;in the worst case, fast meets slow within one full traversal of the list (including the cycle).</span><br>",
            "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Space: O(1):</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;only two pointers are used, no extra memory required.</span><br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6-why-this-pattern-matters-in-interviews",
      "title": "6. Why This Pattern Matters in Interviews",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "This pattern is powerful because it solves problems that look like they need&nbsp;<strong>extra memory or multiple passes</strong>, using just&nbsp;<strong>one pass and no extra space</strong>.",
            "For example, finding the middle usually takes&nbsp;<strong>two passes</strong>, but with fast &amp; slow pointers, it becomes&nbsp;<strong>one pass (O(n))</strong>.",
            "Detecting a cycle or finding its start might seem to require a&nbsp;<strong>hash set (O(n) space)</strong>, but this pattern solves it using just&nbsp;<strong>two pointers (O(1) space)</strong>.",
            "Even problems like finding the&nbsp;<strong>Nth node from the end</strong>&nbsp;can be done in&nbsp;<strong>one pass instead of two</strong>."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "text": "<p><strong>Key Insight:</strong></p><p>Whenever you see a linked list problem involving&nbsp;<strong>positions, cycles, or middle elements</strong>, think of the&nbsp;<strong>fast and slow pointer approach first</strong>.</p><p><strong>Why interviewers love it:</strong></p><p>It shows you can optimize from brute force → optimal (O(1) space, single pass).</p>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7-summary-b",
      "title": "7. Summary",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Core Mechanic:</strong><br>Slow moves 1 step while fast moves 2 steps. This speed difference helps create useful positions in the list.",
            "<strong>Finding Middle:</strong><br>When the fast pointer reaches the end, the slow pointer is at the middle.",
            "<strong>Detecting Cycle:</strong><br>If slow and fast ever meet, a cycle exists. If fast reaches null, there is no cycle.",
            "<strong>Finding Cycle Start:</strong><br>After they meet, reset one pointer to the head. Move both one step at a time they will meet at the start of the cycle.",
            "<strong>Nth from End:</strong><br>Move fast N steps ahead first. Then move both together — when fast reaches null, slow is at the target node."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
